WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.763
Welcome.

2
00:00:00.763 --> 00:00:03.554
This briefing comes from
HR-Driven Identity,

3
00:00:03.554 --> 00:00:07.025
one of the books of the
Federal Modernization Workbook.

4
00:00:07.025 --> 00:00:10.787
It makes one proposal, and we'll
take it through four questions,

5
00:00:10.787 --> 00:00:14.328
the way you'd take it to leadership:
why it matters, what to do,

6
00:00:14.328 --> 00:00:18.238
who has to be involved, and how to
carry it out and know it's working.

7
00:00:18.238 --> 00:00:25.415
Federal Zero Trust policy, OMB
M-22-09 and NIST SP 800-207,

8
00:00:25.415 --> 00:00:29.738
makes identity the place where
every access decision gets made.

9
00:00:29.738 --> 00:00:31.895
This book asks the follow-up question:

10
00:00:31.895 --> 00:00:35.025
where should the facts behind
that identity come from?

11
00:00:35.025 --> 00:00:39.062
The answer is the HR system of
record, and the time to start is now.

12
00:00:39.062 --> 00:00:41.860
First, where this book sits in the series.
